  "worked_solution": "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nHence, since $A$ is orthogonal, we have ${A}^{-1}={A}^{T}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ {A}^{-1}Ax & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\ x & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{15} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{15}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
